  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The overspeed trip was caused by binding and degraded responsiveness of the turbine speed control governor valve assembly. Wear was discovered on the valve stem, valve stem connector, cam crank, and cam crank support. The RCE findings indicate that the governing procedure (MMP-300.015) lacks sufficient detail to ensure proper disassembly, inspection, reassembly, and alignment of the governor valve linkage.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "Inadequate maintenance procedure detail leading to governor valve linkage wear/binding",
    "provisional": true
  },
